===== STAGE99 SOURCE / LOCK / OWNERSHIP AUDIT =====
PASS: TOKEN_USES_EXTERNAL_BOUNDED_RETIRE_STORAGE: token memory is queued externally and no reclaimed intrusive next pointer remains
PASS: TOKEN_RETIRED_BEFORE_BACKEND_CALLBACK: report copies callback inputs, queues token retirement, then calls backend completion
PASS: IRQ_CONTEXT_RELEASE_HOOK_DOES_NOT_FREE: release hook performs only an atomic hook lookup and bounded retire callback
PASS: LOCK_FREE_SEQUENCE_NUMBERED_TOKEN_QUEUE: completion producers reserve sequence-numbered slots; a single consumer reclaims pointers
PASS: RETIRE_PUBLICATION_COUNTER_PRECEDES_ENQUEUE: teardown sees a token in the publication window and the producer never frees it
PASS: POTENTIALLY_BLOCKING_FREE_ONLY_IN_REAPER: deferred single consumer dequeues token, frees storage, then drops outstanding count
PASS: C_BRIDGE_RETURNS_TOKEN_TO_OWNING_ADAPTER: token's retained adapter context receives the retirement node
PASS: LEGACY_AIRPORT_RADIO_OBJECT_HAS_NO_WCL_LINK_DEPENDENCY: shared radio TU uses a registered hook, so the legacy Airport link needs no WCL adapter symbol
PASS: LEGACY_AIRPORT_OBJECT_GRAPH_HAS_COMPILE_ONLY_GATE: shared radio object can be compiled in legacy Airport configuration without invoking the legacy linker
PASS: DUAL_FRONTEND_OBJECT_GATE_DOES_NOT_LINK: the three compile-only recipes only echo success and contain no link/bundle/sign/load commands
PASS: LEGACY_OBJECT_GRAPH_EXCLUDES_WCL_ADAPTER_IMPLEMENTATION: legacy objects stay independent; only the native graph adds the WCL callback adapter
PASS: NATIVE_WORKER_REGISTERS_RELEASER_AFTER_SETUP: only the native worker installs the WCL retire callback before TX activation
PASS: WORKER_CLEARS_RELEASER_AFTER_REAPER_QUIESCENCE: release hook is cleared only after the deferred reaper is stopped and before adapter release
PASS: UNBIND_WAITS_TICKETS_CALLBACKS_AND_RETIRED_TOKENS: adapter cannot release radio/pool until ticket callbacks and token reclamation drain
PASS: ADAPTER_FREE_FAILS_CLOSED_ON_RETIRED_TOKENS: adapter free quarantines rather than destroying a live retire list
PASS: WORKER_ALLOCATES_KERNEL_PRIORITY_REAPER: one native XNU thread-call runs deferred kfree in kernel thread context
PASS: WORKLOOP_SCHEDULES_REAPER_WITH_RESIGNAL_HANDSHAKE: workloop coalesces reaper requests and records a signal that races an active drain
PASS: THREADCALL_DRAINS_ONLY_ON_DEFERRED_PATH: reaper callback drains the adapter list and never re-enqueues itself
PASS: WORKER_STOP_CANCELS_REAPER_BEFORE_RELEASING_OWNERS: event source is removed, pending reaper is joined/freed, then adapter and queue refs drop
PASS: WORKER_STOP_REQUIRES_EMPTY_TICKET_AND_TOKEN_OWNERSHIP: worker refuses to stop while any ticket or token still owns callback state
PASS: CONTROLLER_CHECKS_WORKER_STOP_BEFORE_RELEASE: controller retains worker/queue owners if deferred token cleanup has not finished
PASS: PCI_TX_STATUS_CALLBACK_IS_SYNCHRONOUS_UNDER_IRQ_LOCK: normal PCI report path invokes the native callback before irq_lock release
PASS: FIRMWARE_TX_REPORT_CALLBACK_IS_SYNCHRONOUS_UNDER_REPORT_LOCK: firmware CCX report path also calls tx status while holding tx_report q_lock
PASS: TOKEN_RELEASE_PRECEDES_TICKET_COMPLETION_SIGNAL: token is counted as retired before an unconditional worker wake, including the fail-closed ticket-error path
PASS: SKBUFF_FREE_REPORT_IS_EXACTLY_ONCE: both TX status and early skb free claim a single independently allocated token
